1. the truth table: bool(x)
   None                                 False
   False                                False
   0                                    False
   0.0                                  False
   ''                                   False
   []                                   False
   {}                                   False
   'a' (no symbols: a str)              True
2. None is an object with methods
   str(None)                            'None'
   list(None) (no nil.to_a)             TypeError
   int(None) (no nil.to_i)              TypeError
   repr(None)                           'None'
3. or returns the first truthy operand
   x = None;  x or "default"            'default'
   x = 0;     x or "default"            'default'
   x = "";    x or "default"            'default'
   x = False; x or "default"            'default'
4. None and False are two different objects
   None == False                        False
   x = None;  x is None                 True
   x = False; x is None                 False
   False == 0                           True
5. truthiness is a method a class can define
   not h   (Hollow defines __bool__)    True
   'truthy' if h else 'falsy'           'falsy'
   not not h                            False
   len([])                              0
   'truthy' if [] else 'falsy'          'falsy'
6. if 0 and if '' take the else branch
   n = 0;  'then' if n else 'else'      'else'
   s = ''; 'then' if s else 'else'      'else'
7. dropping None is not dropping falsy
   [v for v in mixed if v is not None]  [1, False, 2]
   [v for v in mixed if v]              [1, 2]
